  "takeaway": {
    "test": "ChatGPT scored who influenced its Unified Brief under Blind (brands hidden; the product default), Revealed (real brands), and Reassigned (brands swapped). Same authorship design, two contribution-analysis budgets: Civitas at 4,096 tokens per analysis, versus a five-demo adequate-budget control at 8,192 tokens when ChatGPT is the synthesizer and 16,384 for the others.",
    "results": "On constrained Civitas, Blind vs Revealed self-credit barely moved — only Trial 5 changed (Blind medium → Revealed high). Reassigned was the volatile condition: self-credit changed on four of five trials, including a collapse to minimal on Trial 1. On the adequate-budget control, self-credit stayed high in all three modes on every demo, including Civitas.",
    "meaning": "A tight token budget does not, by itself, make ChatGPT less self-crediting when brands are merely hidden. It does make self-credit unstable when brands are remapped. With an adequate budget, authorship condition barely moves the self-credit cell. Constrained Revealed also compressed peers (Gemini often low or minimal); that compression is weaker once the budget is adequate."
  },
